{"data": [{"author_id": "2054274215872733184", "created_at": "2026-11-08T11:51:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119397325323800746"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/YHy9APPhL1", "end": 243, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/luisnhenrich/status/2119397325323800746/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119397320508784640", "start": 220, "url": "https://t.co/YHy9APPhL1"}]}, "id": "2119397325323800746", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 33, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "openrouter's auto code scores 74.3% on deep swe and 50.0% on terminal bench 4.0. one router, very different results across workloads. the benchmark closest to your production task matters more than the headline average. https://t.co/YHy9APPhL1", "url": "https://x.com/luisnhenrich/status/2119397325323800746"}, {"author_id": "2884187432", "created_at": "2026-11-08T15:46:48.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119456613488820475"], "id": "2119456613488820475", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 48, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "GPT-5.2 dropped. 70.9% sounds huge until you notice it's OpenAI's own benchmark lol. The swe-bench pro number is 55.6%, up from 50.8%. That’s the one I actually look at. Decent jump, just not the headline jump. Real work tests will tell the rest.", "url": "https://x.com/TheSimonLabs/status/2119456613488820475"}, {"author_id": "2111286354860740608", "created_at": "2026-11-09T01:03:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119596650532577348"], "id": "2119596650532577348", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 42, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Code red worked. OpenAI just shipped GPT-5.2.\n\n70.9% on GDPval — beats human experts on professional tasks, up from 38.8% for GPT-5. SWE-Bench Pro: 55.6%, past Gemini 3 Pro.\n\nMy read: the benchmark war is real, but the test is theirs…\n\nSwitching back? Yes or no?", "url": "https://x.com/StephenzhouX01/status/2119596650532577348"}, {"author_id": "2033883656268484608", "created_at": "2026-11-09T09:30:44.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119724359862378999"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Building a great AI agent isn’t just about choosing the right models. The harness is the architecture surrounding the model. How it renders context, executes actions, manages state, and decides when a…", "display_url": "developer.nvidia.com/blog/six-agent…", "end": 262, "expanded_url": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/six-agent-harness-capabilities-for-higher-model-performance/", "images": [{"height": 1080, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119724371514138625/1RhVAZXo?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1920}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119724371514138625/1RhVAZXo?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 239, "status": 200, "title": "Six Agent Harness Capabilities for Higher Model Performance | NVIDIA Technical Blog", "unwound_url": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/six-agent-harness-capabilities-for-higher-model-performance/", "url": "https://t.co/veSEQkqdgk"}]}, "id": "2119724359862378999", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Same benchmark, half the bill: 82.2% on SWE-bench Verified with GPT-5.5 at 29 model calls and 1.1M tokens per task, against 66 calls and 2.2M for 78.2%. Tool output stays a live object, so the model reads a preview and the cache survives.\nhttps://t.co/veSEQkqdgk", "url": "https://x.com/LeapfrogAgentic/status/2119724359862378999"}, {"author_id": "1904200133933514752", "created_at": "2026-11-09T03:11:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119628795741348239"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 104, "id": "1679186467640205314", "start": 93, "username": "PatronusAI"}]}, "id": "2119628795741348239", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Your agent failed a 40-step run and you can't tell which step broke it. TRAIL Benchmark from @PatronusAI tests how well LLMs locate errors in agent execution traces. It has 148 annotated traces with 841 labeled errors across reasoning, execution and planning, with GAIA and SWE", "url": "https://x.com/EveryDevAi/status/2119628795741348239"}, {"author_id": "2563368151", "created_at": "2026-11-08T01:00:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119233451727491350"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 97, "id": "1392094167522742272", "start": 89, "username": "BAI_AGI"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/M2keDwo4s4", "end": 234, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Motivator_Peter/status/2119233451727491350/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119197841910317056", "start": 211, "url": "https://t.co/M2keDwo4s4"}]}, "id": "2119233451727491350", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 36, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "𝗚𝗣𝗧-𝟱.𝟲 𝗧𝗲𝗿𝗿𝗮 𝗴𝗲𝘁𝘀 𝘄𝗶𝘁𝗵𝗶𝗻 𝟭.𝟮 𝗽𝗼𝗶𝗻𝘁𝘀 𝗼𝗳 𝗦𝗼𝗹 𝗼𝗻 𝗦𝗪𝗘-𝗕𝗲𝗻𝗰𝗵 𝗣𝗿𝗼 𝗳𝗼𝗿 𝗵𝗮𝗹𝗳 𝘁𝗵𝗲 𝗶𝗻𝗽𝘂𝘁 𝗽𝗿𝗶𝗰𝗲 𝗼𝗻 @BAI_AGI.\n\nTerra became generally available on July 9, 2026, and sits between Sol and Luna in the GPT-5.6 line.\n\nHere are https://t.co/M2keDwo4s4", "url": "https://x.com/Motivator_Peter/status/2119233451727491350"}, {"author_id": "3259127768", "created_at": "2026-11-08T16:53:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119473504248533274"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/pWLNt1uy2l", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/kaibrandtAi/status/2119473504248533274/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119473487349735425", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/pWLNt1uy2l"}, {"display_url": "x.com/kaibrandtAi/st…", "end": 322, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/kaibrandtAi/status/2118659623452389698", "start": 299, "url": "https://t.co/djMPVJNElQ"}]}, "id": "2119473504248533274", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 132, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118659623452389698", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "a 9B AI model that codes, sees images and runs on your phone with no internet\n\nit's called Alpie Seed\n\ntrained in 4-bit from day one, so it actually fits on a laptop\n\n61.2% on SWE-bench Verified, a test of fixing real GitHub issues, slightly ahead of Qwen3.5-9B\n\nunderstands https://t.co/pWLNt1uy2l https://t.co/djMPVJNElQ", "url": "https://x.com/kaibrandtAi/status/2119473504248533274"}, {"author_id": "1968416571841462272", "created_at": "2026-11-08T07:36:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119333340696428838"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 213, "id": "1968416571841462272", "start": 204, "username": "169Pi_ai"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/OoolorkM68", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/169Pi_ai/status/2119333340696428838/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119332161425948672", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/OoolorkM68"}]}, "id": "2119333340696428838", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 312, "impression_count": 264626, "like_count": 1019, "quote_count": 46, "reply_count": 84, "retweet_count": 71}, "text": "This Diwali, a little more light from India's AI research community onto the global AI landscape.\n\nIntroducing the latest benchmark results from Alpie Seed, our 9B multimodal reasoning model developed at @169Pi_ai Research.\n\nWe believe the next generation of AI will be shaped not https://t.co/OoolorkM68", "url": "https://x.com/169Pi_ai/status/2119333340696428838"}, {"author_id": "1122555235686342656", "created_at": "2026-11-08T00:38:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119227904043430311"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/VIlW9pwYO4", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/startupnicc1/status/2119227904043430311/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2117673081535897600", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/VIlW9pwYO4"}]}, "id": "2119227904043430311", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "a 24b model now fits on one gpu, and that changed what i keep local.\n\nmistral released devstral small 2 on december 9, 2025, under apache 2.0 with a 256k context window. it’s built for agentic coding, not autocomplete. mistral reports 68% on swe-bench verified, and says it runs https://t.co/VIlW9pwYO4", "url": "https://x.com/startupnicc1/status/2119227904043430311"}, {"author_id": "2570592811", "created_at": "2026-11-08T14:00:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119429739517534491"], "id": "2119429739517534491", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 27, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\"Scores 48.5% on the test.\" Almost every AI launch leads with a benchmark number. Here's what that actually means, in 60 seconds.\n\n→ A benchmark is a standard test: the same questions or tasks given to every model, so scores can be compared\n→ Like an exam, it measures one", "url": "https://x.com/Iammdshohag/status/2119429739517534491"}, {"author_id": "19153682", "created_at": "2026-11-08T09:05:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119355636722835864"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 179, "id": "16363771", "start": 166, "username": "siebelschool"}, {"end": 210, "id": "70795739", "start": 200, "username": "dakuowang"}, {"end": 225, "id": "46477409", "start": 212, "username": "Northeastern"}, {"end": 237, "id": "1490584382360338433", "start": 228, "username": "DiWu0162"}, {"end": 254, "id": "1820204090892419072", "start": 239, "username": "Eric1706291394"}, {"end": 268, "id": "1648471776681394176", "start": 256, "username": "gordonhu608"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/87ERiltSRi", "end": 296, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/guifav/status/2119355636722835864/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119355627726061568", "start": 273, "url": "https://t.co/87ERiltSRi"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/87ERiltSRi", "end": 296, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/guifav/status/2119355636722835864/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119355629592526848", "start": 273, "url": "https://t.co/87ERiltSRi"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/87ERiltSRi", "end": 296, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/guifav/status/2119355636722835864/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119355631538724864", "start": 273, "url": "https://t.co/87ERiltSRi"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/87ERiltSRi", "end": 296, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/guifav/status/2119355636722835864/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119355633363189760", "start": 273, "url": "https://t.co/87ERiltSRi"}]}, "id": "2119355636722835864", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 97, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "An LLM judge flagged about 18% of AI agents' output tokens as removable waste. The task and the harness explain more of that waste than the model does.\n\nHuimin Zeng (@siebelschool), @leoleoasd_cn and @dakuowang (@Northeastern), @DiWu0162, @Eric1706291394, @gordonhu608 and https://t.co/87ERiltSRi", "url": "https://x.com/guifav/status/2119355636722835864"}, {"author_id": "22046059", "created_at": "2026-11-08T22:05:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119551823199502549"], "id": "2119551823199502549", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 4018, "like_count": 30, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Gemini 4 Hyperion references have reportedly appeared in Antigravity’s app and CLI.\n\nA community post describes it as the model coming after Carbon, with a focus on broad knowledge and repeatedly checking its own outputs.\n\nThe same post lists some striking benchmark claims:\n\n•", "url": "https://x.com/deweytn/status/2119551823199502549"}, {"author_id": "95042637", "created_at": "2026-11-09T19:01:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119868080650371308"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/19433068286975…", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/1943306828697550848/status/2119867114450268322", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/y85lnAraHy"}]}, "id": "2119868080650371308", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 1921, "like_count": 13, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2119867114450268322", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Anthropic released two new models today. They are the same model.\n\nClaude Fable 5.2 is the one anyone can use. Claude Mythos 5.2 is the same weights with the safety classifiers lifted, the version Anthropic keeps behind closed doors.\n\nThe split exists because the unrestricted https://t.co/y85lnAraHy", "url": "https://x.com/VaibhavSisinty/status/2119868080650371308"}, {"author_id": "1211668225680793601", "created_at": "2026-11-08T07:18:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119328576063570057"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/OBGCNvcvUv", "end": 296, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/_TeenDifferent/status/2119328576063570057/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119328568190877696", "start": 273, "url": "https://t.co/OBGCNvcvUv"}]}, "id": "2119328576063570057", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "it’s funny…i don’t think we necessarily need arc-agi to find out where ai still struggles lol\n\ncame back to my hometown in india for vacation…and saw one of those spot-the-difference puzzles in eenadu’s sunday magazine. used to solve these a lot as a kid…and they’re still https://t.co/OBGCNvcvUv", "url": "https://x.com/_TeenDifferent/status/2119328576063570057"}, {"author_id": "1742745269886930944", "created_at": "2026-11-09T18:59:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119867575861645630"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 142, "id": "1392094167522742272", "start": 134, "username": "BAI_AGI"}]}, "id": "2119867575861645630", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 19, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Near-Sol coding performance at half the input cost — that's what makes GPT-5.6 Terra worth a closer look.\n\nNow generally available on @BAI_AGI since July 9, 2026, GPT-5.6 Terra sits between Sol and Luna, offering a compelling balance between coding capability and API pricing.", "url": "https://x.com/0xkaizenova/status/2119867575861645630"}, {"author_id": "1799283996171415552", "created_at": "2026-11-07T21:32:30.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119181221682962507"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "B.AI is the foundational economic infrastructure for AI Agents. Access global top-tier AI models anonymously via our borderless payment system. We provide a unified API and settlement network, empowering artificial intelligence with true financial autonomy.", "display_url": "B.AI", "end": 23, "expanded_url": "https://B.AI", "images": [{"height": 1200, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117673859918843905/VijLmBkp?format=png&name=orig", "width": 2400}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2117673859918843905/VijLmBkp?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 0, "status": 200, "title": "B.AI", "unwound_url": "https://B.AI", "url": "https://t.co/iq8sqmJ3cD"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/OuOuxxMQ8b", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/0xfamzy_/status/2119181221682962507/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119181211339796480", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/OuOuxxMQ8b"}]}, "id": "2119181221682962507", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20037, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "https://t.co/iq8sqmJ3cD made Anthropic's Claude Fable 5 callable through its API on June 10, 2026. Fable 5 is part of Anthropic's Mythos class, which the company positions as its most capable model available to the public.\n\nAnthro